// The control: a user type taking a prelude name the prelude does NOT write in
// any surviving item. Nothing breaks, and both compilers accept.
//
// This is the half that says the check is a CHECK and not a ban on the name.
// `HashMap`'s own impl is dropped along with the declaration the user shadowed -
// the drop is matched by kind and takes the impl with it - so no surviving
// prelude item is left mentioning it.
struct HashMap { a: int }

fn main() { println(1); }
